{% extends '@layout/default.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Avoid routing through bootstrap of non existent files{% endblock %}

{% block page_title %}
    <div class="mb-2 text-uppercase small fw-bold text-primary tracking-wider">Dotkernel</div>
    <h1 class="fw-bold text-dark display-6 mb-0">Avoid routing through bootstrap of non existent files</h1>
    <hr class="mt-4 mb-2 opacity-25">
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    <div class="container py-4">
        <div class="row g-4">
            
            {% include '@partial/left-menu.html.twig' %}

            <main class="col-12 col-md-8 col-lg-9">
                <article class="card border-0 shadow-sm p-4 p-md-5 h-100">
                    <header class="mb-4">
                        <h1 class="h2 text-dark fw-bold">Avoid routing through bootstrap of non existent files</h1>
                        <div class="text-muted small">
                            <i class="bi bi-folder2-open me-1"></i> Dotkernel
                        </div>
                    </header>

                    <section class="post-content text-secondary lh-lg fs-6">
                        In some cases you may encounter missing files: images, css or js files.
All those missing files are processed by the current bootstrap: index.php

If the session is set to regenerate on each request, as a normal security measure,
the currently logged user is logged off, because the session ID is different now.

To avoid this, <strong>below</strong> the following line
<pre class="bg-light border rounded p-3 overflow-auto">>RewriteEngine On</pre>
add the line :
<pre class="bg-light border rounded p-3 overflow-auto">>RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} (\.gif|\.jpg|\.png|\.css|\.js)$ </pre>
Save and don't forget to test.

Even though it's a well known fact that real men do not test...
                    </section>
                </article>
            </main>
            
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}